  "tip.relative_moment": "Fill the date above with now, shifted by this much - the command line spells it --at +30d. Months, quarters and years land on the calendar date, not on a fixed number of hours. This row makes one shift and no more, which is why it offers fewer choices than the calculator: business days are absent because a session carries no holiday calendar, and ready-made dates such as a month end are in the Scenario list above.",
  "tip.mode": "How fast the fake clock runs: ×1 is real speed, frozen stops it, and the rest run that many times faster.",
  "tip.scale_duration": "Also speed up timers, sleeps and countdowns inside the app - not just the wall clock.",
  "tip.scale_qpc": "Also speed up QPC-based clocks (Python monotonic, .NET Stopwatch, Java nanoTime). May distort an app that times its rendering off QPC.",
  "tip.embedded": "On by default. An application with a built-in web engine (WebView2, Qt WebEngine) runs its pages in a process the clock hook cannot enter. With this on, the engine is asked to open a local debugging port for the session and the pages follow the session clock through it. Untick it to leave those pages on the real clock and open no port.",
  "tip.force": "Off by default. When the opening verdict says the substitution did not take effect, the target is stopped rather than handed to you, because its evidence would be about the real clock. Tick this to run anyway - the session is then marked unreliable everywhere it appears.",
  "tip.start": "Launch the target under the fake clock. Needs a target and a valid moment.",
  "tip.freeze": "Freeze the fake clock so it stops advancing.",
  "tip.set_speed": "Set any custom speed, e.g. 500.",
  "tip.stop": "Stop the session. The app returns to real time - it is not closed.",
  "tip.jump_to": "Move the fake clock to this date and time, read in the session zone.",
  "tip.copy_summary": "Copy a paste-ready session summary for a ticket.",
  "tip.copy_diagnostics": "Copy the core diagnostics (its stderr) to attach to a support ticket.",
  "tip.base_kind": "Where the calculation starts: today, now, or a specific date.",
  "tip.base_zone": "The zone the start point is read in - today is a different day either side of midnight. This machine's zone is used unless you pick another. Not the same as a to-zone step, which re-expresses the answer.",
  "tip.add_step": "Add a step: shift, snap, nearest business day, set time, or change zone.",
  "tip.calc_calendar": "The holiday and business-day calendar used by business-day and nearest steps.",
  "tip.custom_format": "Render the result with your own format mask (.NET/Java tokens).",
  "tip.analyze": "Paste a date to see how it reads - both interpretations when it is ambiguous.",
  "tip.use_in_substitution": "Send this moment over to Run an app and fill its date. Available only when its zone is one of the offered session zones."
